.github

# Everything below lives in the checkout on a server but has no business in an
# image. The build stage copies the whole context, so each of these used to be
# written into a layer on every build: staged uploads and test videos are
# gigabytes that filled an 8 GB root volume mid-`npm run build`, and the APK is
# installed at runtime from the host, never from inside the image.
.staging
.storage-test
*.tsbuildinfo
*.apk
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# Account configs carry credentials. Leaving them in the context puts secrets
# into the build cache, where `docker history` and a pushed layer can both
# reach them. The names are the ones deploy/provision.sh suggests and the ones
# in use; keep new ones matching these patterns.
my-account*.json
cuenta*.json
*-credentials.json
